WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 size:88% position:44%
-So, a lot of people are
saying now that, look,

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
we basically are down to
two candidates, it seems like.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.472 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And everyone's worried,

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:09.642
if one wins,
will the supporters of the other

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.411 size:88% position:44% line:92%
sort of agree to support

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.512 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the Democratic nominee?

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a question
you get asked a lot.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it safe to assume
that you will support Joe Bide

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he is the nominee?
-Yeah, you know, I think -

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I've said
throughout this entire process

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.791
that what is so important
is that we ultimately unit

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
behind who that
Democratic nominee is,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think
it's a two-way street.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been concerned
by some folks that say,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.068 size:88% position:44%
if Bernie's the nominee,
they won't support him,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.103 line:92%
and the other way around.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.139 line:92%
Right now, November, you know,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is more important
than all of us,

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.175 line:92%
and we really need to make sur

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we defeat Donald Trum
at the polls.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.613 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Assuming and knowing,

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
how insane it's going to get
between now and then.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.317 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, it doesn't seem
like this is going to be

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.120
a laid-back election season.
-It's not going to be chill, no.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.988 line:92%
-No, it's not going to be chill.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.289
It's not going to be like,
"Honey, the debate's on.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's get a glass of wine.
-Yeah. [ Chuckling ]

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:03.363
-One thing that must be
surreal for you is, 2016,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.099 size:75% position:38%
you knocked on doors
for Bernie Sanders.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then two years later,
you get elected congresswoman.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now you are actually
on the stump with Bernie.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you go out on stage
for these giant Bernie rallies

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
does it seem --

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
does it seem as surreal to you
that I imagine it does?

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.946 line:92%
-It's completely surreal.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.082 line:92%
Just, you know, four years ago

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.584 line:92%
I was in the South Bronx,

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as a volunteer,

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
helping organize this massiv
rally in St. Mary's Park,

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
and at the time,
Bernie Sanders was

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the first
Democratic candidates

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
since, I believe,
Robert F. Kennedy

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.996 line:92%
to campaign in the South Bronx

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to have a candidate
that really saw our communit

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.801 size:78% position:39% line:92%
was really impactful,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now to be able
to go out and bear witness

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.273 line:92%
to what so many communitie

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
are experiencing
all across the country

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just very full circle
and gratifying.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.546
-And, obviously, a lot's changed
for you in the four years.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.215 size:75% position:38%
Is it safe to assume
that Bernie hasn't

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
changed at all?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think he's changed
a little bit.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.486 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I think he's changed,

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.122 size:81% position:41%
although, he is famous
for his consistency.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I do think for thos
who are drawn to Bernie,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.459
that is the thing that is
impossible to argue with.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.329
As far as a politician wit
consistency over the years

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.296 line:92%
I mean, he really stands out

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.766
-He does, and he's been fighting
for health care as a right

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
this entire time,
and it's --

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, now that I'm
on the other side in Congres

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.006 size:75% position:38%
and you see how much
pressure there is,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:24.844
you know, to bow to a lot
of special interests...

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:28.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
The fact that he has been
relying on small-dollar donors

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.084
since before the Internet
kind of blows my mind.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like collecting littl
checks this whole time

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
and really committed
to a grassroots movement

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it was way, way harde
than it is even now

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:41.828 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is really phenomenal.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.597 size:88% position:44%
-Another thing that will
have huge implications,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.365 line:92%
not just on this election

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the next decade,
is the census.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you speak about
how you're approaching tha

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just try
to explain to people

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.107 line:92%
exactly how important it is.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:58.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we are all going to get
census forms or a prompt.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.781
We're all going to get maile
a prompt to fill out the censu

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.750 line:92%
in the next two weeks or so,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.019 size:78% position:39%
and so I think what's
really important is

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:06.920 line:92%
that we all fill this out.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.555 line:92%
It happens once every 10 years

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every single person, no matter
your documentation status,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter your housing status,
income, et cetera,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is to be counted,

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and it determines

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
how much our schools are
going to get funded,

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
how much infrastructure
gets invested

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.437
and, of course, how many members
of Congress each community gets.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you get undercounted,
you know --

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.641 line:92%
In some parts of New York City

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
some communities,
the self-reporting is

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
about half of what
we think it should be,

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:37.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that has real impacts
on apportionment of,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.118 line:92%
you know, how many teacher

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.653 line:92%
that your local schools get,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.821 line:92%
so it's really important.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.323 line:92%
It's completely confidential

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's even confidential
within the federal government.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.862 line:92%
Your census data is not shared

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
with any other Federal Agenc
at all.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:56.302
So, don't worry if you're having
a creative living situation.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not gonna be
told to your landlord

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.006 line:92%
or anything crazy like that.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Don't worry.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Totally safe.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
